[2026-11-27T11:58:50Z] note: assumptions: z-score prior window (t-n..t-1, population std); the -4 z stop and the 0.6 correlation filter (126 daily returns) are fixed constants. | BORROW COST ASSUMED (user decision 2026-11-27): the spec says to disable pairs without historical borrow/carry data; there is none, so the short leg pays a constant labelled fee (CONFIG borrow_fee_pct_yr: 0.25 %/yr for these easy-to-borrow ETFs/large caps, 3 %/yr for crypto margin) on its market value per calendar day; stress runs at higher fees are logged after the optimization. Borrow recalls and margin calls are not modelled. | short proceeds earn 0 % and the long leg is paid from the sleeve (no margin interest): conservative carry; total-return (adjusted) closes on both legs, so the short leg pays the dividends it is short (dividend-in-lieu). | gross notional G = 100 % of sleeve equity at entry (equal dollars: G/2 each; ratio 1:beta: long G/(1+beta), short beta*G/(1+beta)); quantities frozen at entry. | same-bar ambiguity: if a leg's stop is touched intrabar, that leg fills at its stop and the other leg at its worst bar extreme (long: low, short: high); if both legs touch, the long leg is assumed first. Gaps through a stop fill both legs at the open. | no new entry on a bar where a position was closed, and no entry when the exit condition (or a forced window end) is true on the signal bar. | costs: library convention (ETFs fee 0.05 % + slippage 0.03 % per fill; crypto 0.10 % + 0.10 %), both legs, entry and exit. | IAU, EWA, EWC and VDE were not in the project; their Yahoo daily history was fetched on 2026-11-27 (src.collectors.yahoo_daily.update, full history) without adding them to config/symbols.yaml, so the nightly job doesn't refresh them.
